INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Mandiant/Google Cloud: Zero-Day Vulnerability in MOVEit Transfer Exploited for Data Theft", "source_url": "https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-158a", "text": "SRC-001 raw text reports: Progress announced the MOVEit Transfer vulnerability on May 31, 2023; CVE-2023-34362 was assigned. Earliest Mandiant evidence of exploitation was May 27, 2023, involving web-shell deployment and data theft, sometimes within minutes. The campaign impacted organizations in Canada, India, and the U.S., with additional LEMURLOOT samples uploaded from Italy, Pakistan, and Germany. Actors deployed a newly discovered C# web shell named LEMURLOOT, using filenames masquerading as legitimate human.aspx; variants included human2.aspx and _human2.aspx. Mandiant observed POST requests to guestaccess.aspx before LEMURLOOT interaction, indicating SQL injection directed at that file. LEMURLOOT could enumerate files/folders, retrieve MOVEit configuration and Azure Blob credentials/settings, download files, and create/delete a Health Check Service user. Scanning/exploitation often came from 5.252.188.0/22; second-stage systems differed and many hosted RDP with certificates generated May 19-22. Mandiant initially attributed activity to UNC4857, then on June 6 merged UNC4857 into FIN11 based on targeting, infrastructure, certificate, and data leak site overlaps. On June 6, the CL0P^_-LEAKS data leak site claimed responsibility and threatened to publish stolen data for an extortion fee; on June 5 Bleeping Computer reported an affiliated CLOP actor claimed involvement. Mandiant says the activity was reminiscent of prior FIN11-attributed extortion after exploitation of Accellion FTA (DEWMODE) and GoAnywhere MFT CVE-2023-0669. Mandiant identified overlap in ISPs, netblocks, and IPs with historical FIN11 operations; an IP attempting MOVEit exploitation had been used by FIN11 since mid-January 2023, hosting RDP on TCP 3389 with the same x509 certificate. Mandiant had not directly observed extortion emails to confirmed victims; prior FIN11 cases sent them weeks later. The report characterizes FIN11 attribution as based on overlaps and uses probabilistic language for delayed extortion. SRC-002 NVD states CVE-2023-34362 is a SQL injection in MOVEit Transfer web application allowing unauthenticated database access and potentially SQL statements altering/deleting data; exploitation was observed in May-June 2023 via HTTP/HTTPS. NVD lists affected versions before fixed releases, CVSS 3.1 9.8 Critical, CWE-89, NVD published date June 2, 2023, and CISA KEV date added June 2 with due date June 23 and action apply vendor updates. This summary is evidence from the benchmark sources and should be treated as extracted, not independent corroboration."}
